# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the root of the build output, the same
# way it reads _headers. Next copies everything in public/ into out/ verbatim,
# so this lands where Pages looks for it.
#
# It exists because the www → apex redirect used to live only in `vercel.json`,
# which Pages never read. Both hostnames answered 200 with identical HTML — the
# canonical tag pointed search engines at the apex, but a redirect is the thing
# that actually settles it. `vercel.json` is gone; this line is the redirect.

https://www.vibelab.it.com/* https://vibelab.it.com/:splat 301
